  "relevance_note": "Official guide describing compaction as a 'loss-aware compression pass' returning opaque encrypted items for continuation across long tool-heavy workflows.",
  "reason_included": "Bridges compaction mechanism with operational constraints (when to compact; prompt stability to avoid drift).",
  "claim_snippets": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "claim_text": "The guide warns to keep prompts functionally identical when resuming after compaction to avoid behaviour drift, and suggests compacting after major milestones rather than every turn.",
      "claim_status": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "claim_text": "The guide emphasises compaction outputs are \"opaque\" and \"designed for continuation, not inspection\", and instructs treating compacted items as opaque (do not parse or depend on internals).",
      "claim_status": "asserted"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "claim_text": "The guide states GPT-5.2 supports response compaction via `/responses/compact`, described as a \"loss-aware compression pass\" over prior conversation state that returns \"encrypted, opaque items\" preserving task-relevant information while reducing token footprint.",
      "claim_status": "asserted"
    }
  ],
